    "text": "in the quiet of the city, where shadows stretch and stretch  \nwe walk through the streets with dreams that never reach the chest  \nthe price of a meal, the cost of a night, the weight of the world  \nwe carry it all, but no one sees the toll it's costing our soul  \n\nthe lines on the faces, the eyes that are tired and worn  \na generation caught in a cycle that no one can break  \nthe promise of progress, the hope that's just a dream  \nwe're stuck in the system, but no one's listening, no one's seen  \n\nthe streets are loud, but the voices are silent  \nthe voices that speak out, the ones that can't be ignored  \nwe're fighting for a future, but the system is slow  \nit's a battle we're losing, but we keep trying to go  \n\nthe economy is broken, the dreams are all gone  \nwe're just another face in the crowd, no one's on the throne  \nbut we'll keep singing, we'll keep fighting, we'll keep striving  \nfor a better life, even if it's just a little bit more  \n\nso let the world know, we're not just a number in the list  \nwe're the people who rise, who fight, who never give up  \neven when the world says no, we'll keep moving forward  \nfor a future that's worth the struggle, and the fight we're going through",
